WEBVTT

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.860
Who are you?

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.360
What's all this?

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.690
Oww...

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.400
I saw an intruder and decided
to teach them a lesson.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.900
I'm not an intruder!

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.400
What are you doing here this late at night?

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.940
Well...

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.030
You wanted to see the Alchemist?

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.320
I wanted to make a return.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.150
A return! A return!

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.320
It's the Alchemist that summoned us, right?

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.190
So he should be able to send us back!

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.030
So I wanted to make a return!

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.780
You mean return a reincarnated author?

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.110
Is that possible?

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.530
Of course not.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.030
No? Really? Why?

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.690
I was hoping for some interesting case to solve.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.230
But I know exactly where this is going.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.780
This place isn't that big!

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:12.280
Too many people would just make it too crowded!

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:17.070
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> and I can handle
the Taints on our own.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.820
So I was thinking the others could just go home.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:23.070
I wondered what all the fuss was about...

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.650
It's you again, red one?

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.400
"Episode 6"

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.530
Dear Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> .

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.780
I am very upset right now.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.320
I'll tell you why...

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:12.790
"Saneatsu Mushanokoji"

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.190
It's finally my turn, huh?

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:16.320
You seem to understand your role.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:22.070
Yes. I know what I must do,
and who I must fight.

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.730
That's the deal, right?

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:24.610
Yes.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:29.820
The Alchemist gives reincarnated
authors the knowledge they need.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.190
It's good to see you again, Mushanokoji- <i>san</i> .

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.480
Oh, Akutagawa- <i>kun</i> ! And Shusei- <i>san</i> !

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.280
You're here too, huh?

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.650
It's good to see you again.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.940
By the way, kitty.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.480
Do you have my room ready?

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.980
No, not yet.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.440
I'd prefer one with a lot of sun.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:52.320
And then hopefully I can put
some plants on the windowsill.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.610
I'll keep that in mind.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.400
Thanks. Can you take care of it for me?

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.940
I'm doing it?

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.190
I'd like a tour of the place, too.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.650
I'll show you around.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:06.820
I'll have Tokuda get
the room ready while you do.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:09.320
It's my job?

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.730
Thank you.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:16.030
No, Mushanokoji's one of the better ones.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.110
The problem is...

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:22.530
Wow, it sure took you forever to call me, huh?

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:22.110
"Naoya Shiga"

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.110
Shiga! So you're here too?

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.860
Oh, you're here too, Musha?

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.280
You've still got that whole
prince look going on, I see.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.320
And you've still got that nasty mouth of yours.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.150
Quiet.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.150
Shiga- <i>san</i> .

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:38.190
Hey, Ryu!

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.480
Good to see you again.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.030
You seem well.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.820
Thanks.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:45.150
I'm glad to see you again.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:49.320
Me too.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.730
Damn it all!

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.400
Why him?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.320
Wow, peach flower boy's in a bad mood, huh?

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.150
Dazai- <i>kun</i> never did like Shiga- <i>sensei</i> .

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.150
Those two just don't get along.

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:14.980
Shiga- <i>sensei</i> always emphasizes
reality in his writing.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.610
"The girl in <i>Setting Sun</i>
doesn't speak properly!"

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.230
I remember him yelling at Dazai over there.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.360
Dazai's mood was just as bad then.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:28.190
Yeah, Dazai was giving him hell back, too.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:33.320
Even though Shiga- <i>sensei</i>
is called "The God of Novels."

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.690
By the way...

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.190
Can't you tell?

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.530
This is Ango Soup.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.940
You're just boiling tuna!

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.530
What else can I do?

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.530
We don't have a lot of ingredients.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.610
If I only had some rice balls...

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.940
Yes. I want rice balls...

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.690
I see.

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:56.190
If you're coming to me to whine,
it must be really bad.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:57.900
It really is bad!

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:03.400
I mean, I don't get along with you,
but he's a thousand times worse!

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.320
And you're saying that to my face, huh?

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.730
But well...

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:12.150
If you really don't like him,
there's only one thing to do.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.610
One thing to do?

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:15.980
You just need to...

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.150
Whisper whisper whisper.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.650
"Rashomon"

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:22.400
Great Teacher Shiga!

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.440
What is it, red one?

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.440
Want to go to the beach?

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:28.820
Why?

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.530
Well, you know...

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:33.190
I wanted to get to know you better!

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:35.730
Then why would you go to the beach?

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:36.820
'Cause the beach is awesome!

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:42.070
It's pretty and the waves are
great and well, we can't go outside...

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.440
But there's a room that's beach-like, I guess.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.320
So...

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.820
It was on a beach in Kamakura, right?

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:49.570
It was famous at the time...

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.360
What was, you ask?

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:56.900
The time the up-and-coming author
Osamu Dazai tried to drown himself to death.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.150
Gulp.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:03.480
If I remember right, the person
with him died and he survived.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:07.530
A lot of people speculated that it was murder.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.860
No!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.730
I was really trying to die too,

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.820
but I didn't...

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.530
This time it's not like that!

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:18.780
This time I've got a plan to kill you!

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.530
Um...

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:25.940
That's not gonna work.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:30.070
So yeah, I'm not going to the beach with you.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:33.190
Or the Minakami Hot Springs
or the Tamagawa Aqueduct.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:35.480
Oh, there you are, Shiga- <i>san</i> .

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:38.820
And Dazai- <i>kun</i> too?

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:40.820
Perfect timing!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.610
"Rashomon"
"Ryunosuke Akutagawa"

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.610
I was just reading your book again.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:48.030
Seriously, where'd you get the idea...

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.530
...that you should publish such a piece of crap?

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.150
<i>Rashomon</i> .

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:56.360
The structure of the book is fantastic.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:08:01.110
The way it arranges time, space,
and characters is brilliant.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.940
And that's why the last part is such a failure.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:07.190
You should've described the protagonist's fate.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:10.480
Yes. But my attempt failed.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:14.400
Because the mind of the
main character doesn't feel real.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:19.980
And because of that, all the characters
are just puppets in a fictional story.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:22.360
You're as harsh as ever, I see.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.820
The writing's a little too florid, too.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:27.940
You shouldn't try to show off when you write.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.480
Shut up!

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:36.190
What do you know about Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:38.480
Do you know about him, then?

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:41.610
You never even knew him back then!

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:42.900
You piece of...

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.610
Dazai- <i>kun</i> , stop!

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.980
You...

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.190
Don't insult Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.570
I'm not.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:54.650
I'm offering criticism.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.400
You always...

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.070
Oww!

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.780
Dazai?

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:06.070
You bastard! What was that for?

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.070
Hey! What are you doing?

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:07.780
--Let me go!
--Calm down!

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.610
I'll make him pay! I'll make him pay!

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.320
This is unheard of.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.030
A fight in the library?

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.440
And you call yourselves authors?

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.650
It's his fault!

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:21.570
You threw the first punch!

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:23.190
Quiet, Shiga.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:25.070
And you calm down too, Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:28.900
This isn't just their problem, Acting Director.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.070
What do you mean?

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:33.280
We're forced to live together
in a confined space.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:36.150
It's natural that we'll experience some stress.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:39.860
Especially given that we only
have a minimum of food.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.030
Not even rice balls...

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.820
I want rice balls...

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.360
That was the Alchemist's decision.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:51.530
If we offer you drink and things to do,
some of you will get too lazy to work.

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:56.110
So we only provide the bare minimum!

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:58.940
So that's why there's nothing but tuna!

00:09:58.940 --> 00:09:59.980
I see.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.610
Because cats like fish.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:05.820
No, it's because tuna is nutritious!

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:08.110
Not because I like it!

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:11.690
No! You love tuna because you're a cat!

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:12.980
I do not love it.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:14.190
I just happen to enjoy it.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.610
That's the same thing!

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:16.900
This is unfair!

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:20.400
I won't ask for much,
but at least give us rice balls!

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:24.190
That's right! Rice balls! Rice balls!

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:29.440
In any event, with nothing to do,
stress is going to build up.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:34.320
And when that happens,
you'll see fights like the one you just saw.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.280
But you know...

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.440
Acting Director.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.980
I have a proposal.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:40.900
A proposal?

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:45.730
The best way to get rid of stress
is to exercise in the open air.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:49.360
So let's farm!

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.570
I knew it...

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:53.230
Let us all farm!

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.400
If we live healthy lifestyles,

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:59.110
we'll be even stronger in combat!

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:02.400
And you saw their obsession
with rice balls, right?

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:08.190
If we don't act, and allow a famine to occur,

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:10.690
there'll be rice riots here!

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.530
Rice riots?

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:17.190
We want rice! We want rice!

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:17.190
I see. That's a serious problem.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.610
What you say makes sense to me.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.730
Are the rest of the authors okay with it?

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.190
Of course.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:26.440
Huh? I don't want to farm.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:29.110
Me either. What a pain.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:30.190
Same.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.940
You may feel resistance at first.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:36.900
But the sense of accomplishment
you get will be addicting!

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:39.030
No, don't just decide that.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.860
I'm sure you're all new, but don't worry.

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:44.030
I'll teach you.

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:45.650
I've got experience.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:46.730
Listen to me.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:49.400
Farming is the only way, Acting Director.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.320
We all agree!

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.820
We do not!

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:54.780
Weren't you listening?

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:59.690
Dazai- <i>kun</i> , I know it's your first time
farming and you're nervous.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:00.980
But don't worry.

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:03.440
Working up a sweat is a wonderful thing!

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:05.150
I'm not "nervous."

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:09.610
I'm sure everyone is looking forward to this!

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:10.860
Are you listening?

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:13.230
Farming, huh?

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.820
Very well. I'll allow it.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.230
Thank you!

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.730
Great, huh, everyone?

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:23.400
Fine. I'll play along.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:26.900
Don't worry, Shiga.
I'll teach you all you need to know.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:29.650
Then I don't have to worry about a thing, huh?

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:31.860
I'm sure I can make something fantastic.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.860
That's something to look forward to.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:40.940
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> , I can harvest
something way better than him!

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.820
Something really big! Or really yummy!

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:46.820
I can't imagine that anybody whose writing is

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.530
as sloppy as yours could harvest anything.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:51.940
What?

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.190
It's a battle, then!

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:54.190
A battle?

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:56.980
A battle to see who can
grow the better vegetable!

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:59.150
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> will taste test!

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:02.530
And if I win, never get close to him again!

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:03.860
Fine.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:06.690
Then if I win... hmm...

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:09.190
How about you shave your head, red one?

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:10.440
Fine.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:13.570
If I lose, the Acting Director shaves his head.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:15.940
Why? This has nothing to do with me!

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.400
This is getting fun.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.690
I'm in.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.480
I accept your challenge!

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.320
I'll show you who's boss!

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:32.280
Wow! I didn't know we had a place like this!

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:35.610
You sure it wasn't made just for today?

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:37.960
"Welcome to the Imperial Library Gardens"

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:36.940
By the Alchemist?

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.400
I'm sure it was.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:42.610
Then shouldn't he just make us some yummy food?

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:44.690
Maybe he doesn't want to spoil us?

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:45.900
Not that I know.

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:49.980
By the way, why are we helping?

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:51.440
This is your fight, right, Dazai?

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:53.730
Don't be like that.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.820
The Reprobrates always stick together, right?

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:59.650
Only when it suits you, huh?

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:01.190
Well, I'm okay with it.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:02.820
We came this far.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.530
The question is, what do we grow?

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.440
They've prepared meat and seasonings...

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:11.150
We need to grow something
that'll go with all that.

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:13.900
What else?

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:14.820
Rice.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:16.190
Rice?

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.400
Yup.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.690
A Japanese man wants rice.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:20.820
Rice for breakfast.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:21.980
Rice for lunch.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:23.070
Rice for dinner!

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.780
That's how we grew up, right?

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:26.940
True.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:30.150
Actually, after all that talk about rice balls,

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:33.320
I'm embarrassed I didn't think of that.

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:36.400
But rice alone is kind of bland, right?

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:39.150
Then grow some veggies, too.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:40.820
But rice is the most important part.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:42.320
We make lots of rice!

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.070
Got it?

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.230
You're really into this rice thing.

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:49.070
I didn't think you were that much of a fan.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:53.030
Rice is what keeps me going, you could say.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:56.820
But you're right.
With rice, we can make all kinds of things.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:59.860
And yummy rice goes with anything.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:04.690
If we make yummy rice, we'll win for sure!

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:06.150
That's right!

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.650
Thanks, Chuya!

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:10.150
We'll do our best to raise that rice!

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:13.030
Yeah! Good luck!

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:16.610
If we can make rice, we can make saké.

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:18.690
Work hard for me...

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:21.780
...and all the alcohol I'm going to drink.

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:23.530
Why am I doing this?

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:27.780
There's nothing wrong with getting
your hands dirty once in a while.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:32.030
That's the wild poet of Kanazawa for you.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.900
So what are we making?

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:36.070
I hadn't actually decided.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:38.190
I've never grown anything in my life.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:40.730
I don't know anything about it.

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:41.820
I guess that makes sense.

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:44.320
You grew up in a rich family.

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:45.360
Squash.

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:49.530
You like squash, right, Sai?

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.570
So why don't we grow squash?

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:53.530
Saku...

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:55.860
Squash? I'm down.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:56.980
Then it's settled.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:02.940
Should I help?

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:06.980
Nope. If the judge helps, it's not fair.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:08.150
What about you?

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.690
I'm an observer.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.480
My hips hurt.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:12.860
No more...

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.820
Hey, get to work.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.230
Right, right.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.280
Oww...

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:25.570
You okay, Saku?

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:31.150
You were a powerful foe in your book.

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.360
Don't be like that.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:36.610
The books are worlds that authors created.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:39.150
Perhaps they enhanced your physical powers.

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:41.400
You don't need to explain!

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:46.690
Dazai- <i>kun</i> , I've got a letter.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:47.730
A letter?

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:48.940
"Osamu Dazai"

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.400
"Saneatsu Mushanokoji"

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:58.820
Dazai- <i>kun</i> , I cannot bear to watch you slack off
while you make your comrades farm.

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:00.690
I'm very mad.

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:03.860
I'll be mad at you directly later.
But now I'm sending a letter.

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:05.900
I'm mad.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:08.230
Dazai- <i>kun</i> !

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:09.900
Why did you need the letter?

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:17.230
Well? Farming's fun, right?

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:18.650
Not at all.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:22.440
I can't understand why you
would volunteer to do this.

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:26.110
Humans have a duty to do physical labor.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.650
Tolstoy, right?

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:30.730
But how are you supposed to write, then?

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:34.940
You can write while you farm, if you ask me.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:36.650
I don't know how.

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:39.400
You can do this if you want.

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:41.150
I'll support you.

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:45.780
That's right. You spent a lot
of money to support me.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.150
'Cause you begged me for it.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:49.480
Did I?

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.780
It's growing!

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:59.820
This accelerator's amazing.

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:03.030
Okay! Tomorrow's harvest day!

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.480
I can't wait!

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:08.570
Thanks for working so hard for my saké...

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:12.570
Now I just have to harvest it before
they do, early in the morning...

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.690
Wh-What?!

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:21.860
Why is it all harvested?!

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:26.690
Who did it?! Who?! Who?!

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:26.690
What's wrong, Chuya?

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:27.820
The rice...

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:29.730
Hey, where's Ango?

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:37.820
Wh-What is this?!

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.730
Oh. You're late.

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:41.730
D-Don't tell me...

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:45.820
Yeah, I got up in the middle of the night
and wanted to make some curry.

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:48.280
And we had plenty of rice, so I did.

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:49.400
Enough for a hundred people.

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:50.730
A hundred people?!

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:55.320
Did you use all the vegetables and rice
we raised in the curry?

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:56.230
Yup!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.860
Now what do I do?!

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:02.480
I was going to use all that for our battle!

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:05.150
Well, he made it, and that's it.

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:06.650
Let's eat.

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:07.820
And now you're eating it!

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:10.730
Wh-What is this?

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:13.190
<i>Y-Yokan</i> ? Maybe.

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:15.690
Yes. I made it with the squash.

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.690
You like <i>yokan</i> , right, Sai?

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:20.070
For me?

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:21.110
Here.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.230
Thank you, my friend!

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:31.650
H-How did you make this, Saku?

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.530
Well...

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:36.820
I steamed the squash I harvested,

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.820
added in a lot of sugar...

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.070
And what else?

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:45.860
Just a few of your favorites
as a secret ingredient...

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:51.570
How do you like it?

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:53.900
Sai?

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:55.730
Sai! Sai!

00:19:57.980 --> 00:20:00.150
I will now announce the winner!

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:04.690
You ready, Akutagawa- <i>kun</i> ?

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:05.940
Of course!

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:09.820
Now, announce the winner
of the farming food battle!

00:20:09.820 --> 00:20:11.150
The winner is...

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:18.980
The winner is Tokuda and Shimazaki's team!

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:22.730
We won!

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:23.980
We sure did!

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:25.650
Where did you come from?

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:26.940
When did you get here?

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:28.820
How rude!

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:30.570
We were here the whole time.

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:32.940
Right next to you.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:37.400
Shusei's hometown, Kanazawa,
is famous for its curry.

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:40.820
It was delicious curry that
really brought out the flavor.

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.280
Did you see them?

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:43.860
Nope.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:47.860
You're so boring that they missed me too.

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:49.610
It's my fault?

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:51.780
And don't call me boring!

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:53.230
What a ridiculous ending.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.980
Do you hate Shiga- <i>san</i> that much?

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:04.150
I do!

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:07.650
After what he said about your stories...

00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:10.530
I think he was right.

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:13.190
Shiga- <i>san</i> is amazing.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:17.690
His description of a scene
is more real than a photograph.

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:23.070
His descriptions of a character's mind
reveal the hidden-most thoughts of a man.

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:26.860
His novels are the real thing.

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:29.610
Mine aren't.

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:32.730
Art is something beyond my comprehension.

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:34.110
That's not true...

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:37.190
Such novels are worthless...

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:39.440
So maybe they should just be...

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.440
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:45.610
Wh-What is this?

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:56.780
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:00.920
"Portrait of Hell"

00:23:31.530 --> 00:23:33.110
Literary Gourmet!

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:35.940
<i>Karei</i> Rice, Everybody's Favorite Campside Food!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:37.890
"Imperial Library Camping Trip"

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:38.440
We all went camping!

00:23:38.440 --> 00:23:41.230
Camping? Where is this?

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:42.900
"Our Campground"

00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:43.230
Oh, it's in the library.

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:45.820
We started a fire and made campfire food!

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:48.070
You didn't do anything, though!

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:50.360
Barbecue! Ajillo! <i>Karei</i> [Flounder]!

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:54.410
"Stewed <i>Karei</i> "
"A white fish long-favored in Japan.
Best with a little ginger."

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:53.400
You mean stewed fish? Not curry rice?

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:55.110
On a camping trip?

00:23:54.660 --> 00:24:00.830
"It was good."

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:58.730
The <i>karei</i> and rice we had
on our camping trip was delicious.

00:23:58.730 --> 00:24:00.610
But you didn't eat it all...
